{"member_key":"rs-2591","house":"Rajya Sabha","kind":"special_mentions","records":[{"title":"Demand for safeguarding Bihar's water interests on renewal of the Farakka Water Treaty.","date":"2026-08-06","details":[["Date","06/08/2026"],["Session","271"],["Ministry","EXTERNAL AFFAIRS"],["Reply","No Reply"]],"links":[{"label":"Official source","url":"https://rsdoc.nic.in/memberGetdata/Get_SpecialMentionmemberwise?mpcode=2591"}]},{"title":"Need for convergence of ‘One District One Product (ODOP)’ and ‘Mera Gaon Meri Dharohar (MGMD)’.","date":"2026-02-04","details":[["Date","04/02/2026"],["Session","270"],["Ministry","COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY"],["Statement","Shri Sanjay Kumar Jha: ODOP (One District\r\nOne Product) is an ?elaborately thought out undertaking of DPIIT (Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade)\r\nto transform local specialties into global brands, supporting\r\nartisans, farmers, and small enterprises while preserving India?s rich cultural\r\nheritage. ODOP products are showcased and promoted internationally through\r\ntrade fairs, exhibitions, e-commerce platforms, and diplomatic channels,\r\nthereby enhancing India?s export footprint and brand value. Bihar has shown\r\ntremendous potential under ODOP scheme. Each district has strategically\r\nidentified export-oriented products ranging from pharmaceuticals from Siwan, to\r\nbamboo products from Samastipur, as well as the globally acclaimed Shahi Litchi\r\nand Lahthi fruits of Muzaffarpur, and Katarni rice and silk from Bhagalpur, Tea\r\nfrom Kishangarh to name a few. While ODOP as a stand-alone initiative promises\r\nto transform the local economy of a district, when combined with yet another\r\ninitiative the Mera Gaon Meri Dharohar (MGMD) programme, it could help herald\r\nor reinforce knowledge of India?s cultural traditions, across the globe. MGMD?s\r\nmapping of the cultural ecosystem in India?s villages carries the potential to\r\nenrich ODOP product narratives by embedding history, rituals and local identity\r\ninto product branding. Thus, each ODOP export could be showcased as a ?living\r\ncultural artefact?. Village lores, legends and verified traditional knowledge\r\ndocumented under MGMD can form the cultural backbone of ODOP promotion. ????????? Villages\r\nmapped under MGMD for their distinctive crafts, art forms or rituals could be\r\nformally clustered as ODOP?Heritage spaces. Such spaces can integrate ODOP\r\nexport production with cultural exhibition zones and community museums. This\r\nmodel links livelihood generation with the preservation of intangible cultural\r\nheritage.I urge Government to look into it.\n(ENDS)"],["Reply","No Reply"]],"links":[{"label":"Official source","url":"https://rsdoc.nic.in/memberGetdata/Get_SpecialMentionmemberwise?mpcode=2591"}]},{"title":"Demand to make Nalanda University as a global research hub.","date":"2025-12-04","details":[["Date","04/12/2025"],["Session","269"],["Ministry","EXTERNAL AFFAIRS"],["Statement","Shri Sanjay Kumar Jha: &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2330;&#2368;&#2344;\r\n&#2344;&#2366;&#2354;&#2306;&#2342;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2361;&#2366;&#2352;\r\n&#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350;\r\n&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352;&#2306;&#2346;&#2352;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306;\r\n&#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2352;&#2366;&#2359;&#2381;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351;\r\n&#2358;&#2376;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2339;&#2367;&#2325; &#2310;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344;-&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344;\r\n&#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368;&#2325; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366;\r\n&#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; 2010 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2357;&#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2354;&#2351;\r\n&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2369;&#2344;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2346;&#2344;\r\n&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&